    "content": "Somalia's National Intelligence and Security Agency (NISA), supported by international partners, carried out a planned operation in the village of Bur Saruur, located in the Middle Shabelle region. The operation resulted in the deaths of 12 Al-Shabaab fighters, according to a statement released by NISA.\n\nThe village of Bur Saruur is situated approximately 2 kilometers southeast of the Ali-Gadud area. The operation specifically targeted a location where Al-Shabaab militants were gathering. During the raid, military equipment and hideouts used by the group were also destroyed.\n\nThis operation is part of ongoing efforts by Somali security forces to weaken Al-Shabaab's presence in the region. The group has been waging an insurgency for years, frequently targeting government officials, security personnel, and civilians. NISA has intensified its operations against Al-Shabaab in recent months, often coordinating with international allies.\n\nThe Middle Shabelle region has been a focal point of these operations, as it serves as a strategic area for both the government and the militant group. The success of such operations is often measured by the disruption of Al-Shabaab's ability to plan and execute attacks.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this operation underscores the continued volatility in parts of Somalia and the importance of sustained support for security efforts. Many in the diaspora have family members in affected regions and closely follow developments. The international partnership in this operation also highlights the role of foreign support in Somalia's fight against terrorism.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/25/nisa-oo-howlgal-ka-fulisay-shabeellaha-dhexe/",
